  "contributor": "eoltracker-agent",
  "notes": "The vendor support pages publish per-minor-version tables with day-precision Release Date (GA) and End of Premium Support (EOL) columns. The v7 support page lists v6.x and v7.x versions; the v8 support page lists v7.x and v8.x versions. EOL here is the 'End of Premium Support' date as defined by the vendor: 'the last day you may receive technical assistance for using and integrating the editor.' The EOL is the terminal support date — no separate eossec or eos dates are published. Day-precision ISO dates are used directly."
